@startuml SatIntel_User_Workflow

skinparam backgroundColor #0F172A
skinparam defaultFontColor #E2E8F0
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam defaultFontName Inter

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #94A3B8
  ArrowFontColor #94A3B8
  ArrowThickness 2
  LifeLineBorderColor #475569
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #1E293B
  ParticipantBorderColor #06B6D4
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #1E3A5F
  ParticipantFontColor #E2E8F0
  ParticipantFontStyle bold
  GroupBorderColor #475569
  GroupBackgroundColor #1E293B22
  DividerBorderColor #334155
  DividerFontColor #94A3B8
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #1C2432
  BorderColor #10B981
  FontColor #E2E8F0
}

title <font size=18 color=#06B6D4><b>SatIntel — User Journey Sequence Diagram</b></font>

actor "<font color=#EF4444><b>User</b></font>\n(Municipal Officer)" as User #1C1917
participant "<font color=#F59E0B><b>Frontend</b></font>\n(React + Deck.gl)" as FE #1A1F2E
participant "<font color=#8B5CF6><b>Backend</b></font>\n(FastAPI)" as BE #1E293B
participant "<font color=#10B981><b>ML Engine</b></font>\n(scikit-learn)" as ML #1C2432
database "<font color=#3B82F6><b>Data Store</b></font>\n(JSON + PostgreSQL)" as DB #1E293B
participant "<font color=#06B6D4><b>GEE</b></font>\n(Satellite API)" as GEE #1E3A5F
participant "<font color=#F97316><b>NASA FIRMS</b></font>\n(Fire API)" as FIRMS #1C1917

== <font color=#F59E0B>Phase 1: Landing & Authentication</font> ==

User -> FE : Visit website
FE -> FE : Play 240-frame\nscroll animation
FE -> User : Show Landing Page\n(after scroll complete)
User -> FE : Click "Get Started"
User -> FE : Enter name, email, password
FE -> BE : POST /auth/signup
BE -> DB : create_user()\n(bcrypt hash)
DB --> BE : user object
BE --> FE : { token, user }
FE -> FE : Store JWT in localStorage
FE -> User : Redirect to /dashboard

== <font color=#06B6D4>Phase 2: Dashboard — Environmental Overview</font> ==

User -> FE : Select city from dropdown\n(e.g., Surat)
FE -> BE : GET /analytics/summary/surat
BE -> DB : _load_data(LST, surat)\n_load_data(NDVI, surat)\n_load_data(NO2, surat)\n_load_data(SOIL_MOISTURE, surat)
DB --> BE : JSON data arrays
BE -> ML : detect_anomalies()\nfind_hotspots()
ML --> BE : anomalies + hotspots
BE --> FE : { statistics, anomaly_count,\nhotspot_count per param }

FE -> BE : GET /satellite/timeseries/LST?city=surat
BE -> DB : Load + harmonize (IDW 1km)
DB --> BE : timeseries data
BE --> FE : { timeseries: [{date, value}...] }

FE -> BE : GET /maps/heatmap/LST?city=surat
BE --> FE : { points, raw_points, min, max }

FE -> FIRMS : Fetch VIIRS active fires\n(Gujarat region, last 48h)
FIRMS --> FE : CSV → parsed fire points

FE -> FE : Render Dashboard:\n• Stats Cards\n• MapLibre + Deck.gl Map\n• Recharts timeseries
FE -> User : Display interactive dashboard

note over FE
  **Map Features:**
  • 5 basemap styles (Dark/Satellite/Terrain/Streets/Light)
  • 5 viz modes (Heatmap/3D Hexbin/Grid/Scatter/Contour)
  • 8 data layers (LST/NDVI/NO₂/SO₂/CO/O₃/Aerosol/SM)
  • Wildfire overlay (NASA FIRMS live data)
  • 3D tilted view with rotation
end note

== <font color=#10B981>Phase 3: ML Analytics — Deep Dive</font> ==

User -> FE : Navigate to Analytics
User -> FE : Select parameter (e.g., NO₂)
FE -> BE : POST /analytics/anomalies\n{ parameter: "NO2", city: "surat" }
BE -> DB : Load NO₂ data for Surat
BE -> ML : IsolationForest(contamination=0.08)
ML --> BE : anomalies with severity scores
BE --> FE : { anomalies[], anomaly_count }

FE -> BE : POST /analytics/trends
BE -> ML : ARIMA(2,1,1) → 30-day forecast
ML --> BE : { historical, forecast, direction }
BE --> FE : trend data

FE -> BE : POST /analytics/hotspots
BE -> ML : DBSCAN(eps=0.02, min_samples=2)
ML --> BE : { hotspots[], cluster_count }
BE --> FE : hotspot clusters

FE -> User : Display:\n• Anomaly list with severity badges\n• Trend chart with forecast overlay\n• Hotspot cluster map (Deck.gl)

== <font color=#EF4444>Phase 4: Action Plan Generation</font> ==

User -> FE : Click "Generate Action Plan"
FE -> FE : Show progress steps:\n1. Fetching data...\n2. Anomaly detection...\n3. Trend analysis...\n4. Hotspot clustering...\n5. Generating plan...

FE -> BE : POST /action-plan/generate\n{ city: "surat", parameters: [...] }

BE -> DB : Load all params for Surat
BE -> ML : Run all 3 models × 4 params
ML --> BE : Full analysis results

BE -> BE : _generate_template_plan()\n• City-dynamic (notable_areas)\n• Findings from real data\n• Risk matrix\n• Recommendations\n• KPI targets

BE --> FE : Complete action plan JSON

FE -> User : Render municipal-grade report:\n• Executive Summary\n• Key Findings (4)\n• Risk Assessment Matrix\n• Priority Zones (with coords)\n• Recommendations (5)\n• Monitoring Framework

User -> FE : Click "Export as PDF"
FE -> FE : Generate PDF client-side
FE -> User : Download PDF report

== <font color=#94A3B8>Phase 5: Ongoing Monitoring</font> ==

User -> FE : Switch city → Ahmedabad
FE -> FE : CityContext update\n→ all components re-fetch
FE -> User : Dashboard auto-refreshes\nwith Ahmedabad data

note over User, GEE
  **Data Refresh Cycle:**
  GEE data re-fetched quarterly via:
  python notebooks/01_gee_data_fetch.py
  (14 cities × 10 parameters)
end note

@enduml
